# Files that are run on a Linux machine keep Linux line endings, whatever the
# machine they are edited on.
#
# Written after a carriage return reached a node inside a shebang: the agent
# was copied straight from a Windows checkout, and the kernel looked for an
# interpreter called "python3\r". Nothing in the file was wrong; the checkout
# was. Without this, that is a mistake every Windows checkout makes again.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
